[Elasticsearch](https://elastic.co/elasticsearch) can now turn PDFs, scanned pages, images, and web pages into clean Markdown, with one[inference](https://www.elastic.co/docs/explore-analyze/elastic-inference) call. The new` document_extraction` task type in[Elastic Inference Service (EIS)](https://www.elastic.co/docs/explore-analyze/elastic-inference/eis) provides access to Jina Reader capabilities through a preconfigured` .jina-reader` inference endpoint


. You can send a URL or a Base64 file and get Markdown back. At the core of the document_extraction is the recently released[jina-ocr-v1](https://jina.ai/models/jina-ocr-v1/) , which is currently the[highest rated optical character recognition (OCR) model on the olmOCR-bench under 600 million active parameters](https://huggingface.co/datasets/allenai/olmOCR-bench?leaderboard_base_model=true&leaderboard_task_id=overall) . Scans, tables, and formulas in more than 100 languages come back readable. Tables return as HTML, and formulas come back as LaTeX. The document_extraction handles format conversion and multipage documents, up to 35 pages per request. On[EIS](https://www.elastic.co/docs/explore-analyze/elastic-inference/eis) , billing and authentication are managed for you, as is scaling. Store the resulting Markdown to a[semantic_text](https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/semantic-search-simplified-semantic-text) field, for embedding


, or to a[semantic field](https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/semantic-field-multimodal-search-elasticsearch) , if you’re incorporating other modalities, such as images from the documents. The extracted content can be indexed into Elasticsearch and embedded for[semantic and hybrid search](https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/hybrid-search-elasticsearch)[or context engineering for agents](https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/context-engineering-for-agents) , as well as[AI indices](https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/ai-index-building-context-agents) . It can then be used in AI search and[retrieval augmented generation (RAG) applications](https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/rag-pipeline-scanned-pdf-jina-ocr) .` document_extraction` is in technical preview in Elasticsearch 9.6 and is available for all Enterprise subscriptions as part of EIS.


Using` document_extraction` through EIS consumes[Elastic Consumption Units (ECUs)](https://www.elastic.co/docs/deploy-manage/cloud-organization/billing/ecu) .` document_extraction` is available for Elastic Cloud Hosted and Elastic[Serverless](https://www.elastic.co/cloud/serverless) deployments, as well as Elastic Self-Managed deployments with Cloud Connect. Pricing is $0.075 per 1 million tokens. OCR and other specialized extraction modes may increase token


consumption rates (for example, 40x for OCR).


## The difference between document_extraction and directly calling jina-ocr-v1on EIS


In September 2026, we launched[jina-ocr-v1 as a managed model](https://www.elastic.co/search-labs/blog/ocr-model-jina-ocr-v1-document-parsing) on EIS. document_extraction provides similar capabilities, along with support for inputs like URLs, PDFs, documents, and images via a single endpoint. There are differences, however, and you may wish to choose one or the other, depending on your use case. Using jina-ocr-v1 directly is suitable when you require reading text from images or scans with low latency


. document_extraction provides a wider set of capabilities for managing different formats and document


sizes when powerful OCR capabilities aren’t needed.


## Create a document extraction inference endpoint


Every Elasticsearch deployment with access to EIS includes a preconfigured` .jina-reader` endpoint, so you can start right away, as shown in the following examples.


If you use the same settings frequently, you can define your own endpoint with these settings preconfigured. For example, the code below creates a Jina Reader endpoint that always uses the` pdf+` setting, so you don’t have to specify changes from the preset for each request:


```text
PUT _inference/document_extraction/my-reader
{
"service": "elastic",
"service_settings": {
"model_id": "jina-reader"
},
"task_settings": {
"parameters": {
"preset": "pdf+"
}
}
}
```


## Convert a web page to Markdown


The simplest case is turning a web page into clean Markdown. When you pass the endpoint a URL, it fetches and renders the page, stripping the navigation and boilerplate, and then returns the content.


```text
POST _inference/document_extraction/.jina-reader
{
"input": [
{
"content": {
"type": "html",
"format": "url",
"value": "https://example.com/"
}
}
]
}
```


## Pass a URL instead of uploading the file


You don’t have to download a document first. Each content type takes a type and a format, and for most of them, you can pass a URL to a public website or file instead of the document itself:


**Content type**


` **type**`


**Supported**` **format**`


**Notes**


Web page


` html`


` url` only


Fetches and renders the page


PDF


` pdf`


` url` ,` base64`


Up to 35 pages per request


Image


` image`


` url` ,` base64`


Scanned pages, photos, screenshots


Passing a URL keeps the request small and the documents out of Elasticsearch until you index the extracted content.


## Choose between text extraction and OCR


document_extraction has several extraction pipelines. Fast text extraction works on HTML pages and on the text layers embedded in PDFs. For higher quality results, you can have the document fully rendered and processed by` jina-ocr-v1` . Additional options control the process. (For a list, see the[Elastic documentation](https://www.elastic.co/docs/explore-analyze/elastic-inference/eis#document-extraction-on-eis) .) The main choice is between text extraction and` jina-ocr-v1` , and text extraction is the default:


```text
POST _inference/document_extraction/.jina-reader
{
"input": [
{
"content": {
"type": "html",
"format": "url",
"value": "https://elastic.co/"
}
}
]
}
```


To use` jina-ocr-v1` , set a preset in the` parameters` object of the optional` task_settings` field, as described in[Change how documents are extracted](https://www.elastic.co/docs/explore-analyze/elastic-inference/eis#document-extraction-parameters) :


```text
POST _inference/document_extraction/.jina-reader
{
"input": [
{
"content": {
"type": "html",
"format": "url",
"value": "https://elastic.co/"
}
}
],
"task_settings": {
"parameters": {
"preset": "ocr"
}
}
}
```


## Extract text from an image


Extracting text from an image is straightforward with the new` document_extraction` task type:


```text
POST _inference/document_extraction/.jina-reader
{
"input": [
{
"content": {
"type": "image",
"format": "base64",
"value": "data:image/png;base64,<base64-encoded image>"
}
}
]
}
```


Example image:


Extracted Markdown:


```text
Good King Wenceslas looked out,
On the Feast of Stephen,
When the snow lay round about,
Deep and crisp and even;
Brightly shone the moon that night,
Though the frost was cruel,
When a poor man came in sight,
Gathering winter fuel.
```


## Convert PDFs to Markdown


### Convert a single-page PDF to Markdown


Most PDFs are born digital. They come from word processors or other office software and contain an embedded text layer, so the content can be extracted directly without OCR. This is the easiest way to process a PDF with document_extraction in EIS.


```text
POST _inference/document_extraction/.jina-reader
{
"input": [
{
"content": {
"type": "pdf",
"format": "url",
"value": "https://pdfobject.com/pdf/sample.pdf"
}
}
]
}
```


### Convert a multipage scanned PDF with OCR


Scanned documents and PDFs with complex layouts, like the jina-ocr-v1 paper below, need a more powerful pipeline. Here, we use the` pdf+` preset, which combines layout detection with` jina-ocr-v1` and the` page` parameter to extract only the first three pages. OCR and layout pipelines bill per page. If you don’t set` page` , document_extraction extracts the first 35 pages, which is the most it handles in a single request.


```text
POST _inference/document_extraction/.jina-reader
{
"input": [
{
"content": {
"type": "pdf",
"format": "url",
"value": "https://export.arxiv.org/pdf/2609.03181"
}
}
],
"task_settings": {
"parameters": {
"preset": "pdf+",
"page": "1-3"
}
}
}
```


## Get started with document extraction in Elasticsearch 9.6


Ready to get started? Document_extraction is available in technical preview as part of Elasticsearch 9.6,[now available on Elastic Cloud](https://cloud.elastic.co/registration) .
